        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-245.1529" YPOS="1511.2104" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="194968096" PTYPE="6" WIDTH="231.243" HEIGHT="118.676" FRTYPE="3" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1.7208" PCOLOR2="Black" PLINEART="1" path="M0 0 L231.243 0 L231.243 118.676 L0 118.676 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L231.243 0 L231.243 118.676 L0 118.676 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-245.1529" gYpos="3175.2168" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="112.724392307692" YPOS="928.05" OwnPage="1" ItemID="194956768" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="234.462307692308" HEIGHT="268.95" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L234.462 0 L234.462 268.95 L0 268.95 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L234.462 0 L234.462 268.95 L0 268.95 L0 0 Z" gXpos="112.724392307692" gYpos="928.05319999998" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="Bertie Wooster"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="In nomine comoedia"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="1. When the humorist writes, he ought to will the entire piece be one of intelligibility."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="2. Satire cannot be understood as merely the presence of references and proper nouns; artificial intelligence, Farnam Jahanian, Palantir, and Charlie Kirk do not a joke make."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="3. When references are to be made, timeliness is of utmost importance."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="4. More generally, timing is essential. In writing, this is achieved through punchiness and restraint."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="5. They preach only false doctrines who teach that a sentence becomes funnier by being made longer, stranger, and more subordinatedly claused."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="6. A joke explained is a joke better left unstated."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="7. Similarly, it is certain that a joke, once made, need not be made again in the following sentence, nor in the sentence after that, nor as a concluding callback whose only merit is persistence."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="8. Those satirists are in error who say that if a line is weak, it may be redeemed by placing it within quotation marks and attributing it to a sophomore in SCS."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="9. No rule of humor is firmly true and to attempt matters of the heart is ever difficult."/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <ITEXT CH="9.5. Blessed be all those who attempt humor, however feeble. "/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <para ALIGN="1"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="440.5022" YPOS="211.7612" OwnPage="0" ItemID="194979424" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="257.6845" HEIGHT="468.9263" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="2" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L257.684 0 L257.684 468.926 L0 468.926 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L257.684 0 L257.684 468.927 L0 468.927 L0 0 Z" gXpos="440.5022" gYpos="211.7612" gWidth="268.411518861382" gHeight="214.4468" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="WP"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" CH="Old"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="0" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Me and the freshman from the other page have one thing in common: we have never been to Spring Carnival. If you’re a first year Master's student, you need to lock in, because there’s a good chance your program (which also has a 1 in 5 chance of having the word “AI” in it) runs for three semesters. This means that this might be your one and only chance to participate in Carnival as a student. If you’re a Ph.D. student, why are you reading this? Go back to your lab, bitch. If you did your undergrad here and came back for more, fuck you for being smarter than me. "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    The trick to enjoying Carnival is to never forget the cardinal rule of graduate school: you are Old. Your age doesn’t matter, and I would like to point out that this is the only context in which you get to use that phrase. You could be 21, freshly out of undergrad, and younger than current seniors. Doesn’t matter. You are Old. The faster you accept this, the higher your chance of being able to enjoy yourself. Being Old shifts how people look at you for doing certain things because you’re expected to have some of your shit together. A good example of this is day drinking. Be a responsible adult: hide your vodka in a water bottle, and be discreet about it. You are past the age where people will trust you enough to take a swig from it, anyway. "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    This leads to the next point of Carnival. How do you bond with the undergraduates here? For the first time, you might have to interact with the half of the school’s population that you’ve managed to avoid. Fortunately for you, I have spent the better part of the year working undercover at this awful campus publication in order to figure them out. My research has led me to one one conclusion: they are people too. They might be a bit smarter or richer than you, but that doesn’t change the fact that you should treat them like you would a normal person. If you want to be friendly and get some good memories from this event, be yourself! Being mean to people has never led me astray. Don’t let self-doubt get in the way of you walking up to a teenager and telling them that their parents don’t love them, or asking if they’re “supposed to look like that.” People will find you hilarious."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    That being said, if you're a student in a short program, you don’t really have the option to be able to bounce back from a terrible semester. That means that if you’re already stressed out, you might feel the urge to skip out on everything, and not even waste an hour strolling on the lawn admiring the commotion. Listen to that urge. When your time comes, you’ll want to  rest assured knowing that you got through graduate school without a single “B”. Nobody has ever laid on their deathbed and gone, “Man, I wish I had done more things.” "/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="113.4367" YPOS="1204" OwnPage="1" ItemID="194982256" PTYPE="2" WIDTH="236.75" HEIGHT="298.25" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="0.179356060606061" LOCALSCY="0.179356060606061" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="0" RATIO="1" Pagenumber="0" PFILE="5.7 images/781290C4-6FD5-4CEB-B1F2-49AE920B005F.jpeg" IRENDER="0" EMBEDDED="0" path="M0 0 L236.75 0 L236.75 298.25 L0 298.25 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L236.75 0 L236.75 298.25 L0 298.25 L0 0 Z" gXpos="113.4367" gYpos="1204" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="580.1258" YPOS="676.725" OwnPage="0" ItemID="194993584" PTYPE="2" WIDTH="126.53125" HEIGHT="126.80625" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="0.105442708333333" LOCALSCY="0.105442708333333" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="0" RATIO="1" Pagenumber="0" PFILE="5.7 images/CMU_ReadMe_Donate_Link.png" IRENDER="0" EMBEDDED="0" path="M0 0 L126.531 0 L126.531 126.806 L0 126.806 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L126.531 0 L126.531 126.806 L0 126.806 L0 0 Z" gXpos="580.1258" gYpos="676.725" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1"/>
    </DOCUMENT>
